target: skills/review/review-loop/context.sh
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/context-sizing.test.sh
expect: FAIL  one entry short of the regrowth margin is not due
why:    the sweep trigger is a COUNT but the sweep evicts by RELEVANCE, so a file already swept to 36 has nothing new to drop at 40 and re-arming on the bare count spawns a compaction agent on every run for zero evictions. The one run this was built from went 42 to 36 with zero dead-path and zero stale evictions, and four entries added later in the same run re-armed it immediately; nothing durable records that run, so it is one observation rather than a measurement. The post-sweep count travels in the learnings file so the cost scales with growth.
--- old
        and (swept_entries is None
             or learn_entries >= min(swept_entries + LEARN_REGROWTH, LEARN_CAP - 2))),
--- new
        and True),
